  "notes": "KNOWN GAP: the JNI snapshot layout (ghostty_jni.cpp, Wave 3) exposes only GHOSTTY_CELL_DATA_CODEPOINT (the base codepoint). Ghostty's C API also has a GhosttyCellContentTag.codepoint_grapheme tag for cells carrying combining marks, but Wave 3's shim does not surface the attached grapheme codepoints. This fixture therefore only asserts what the current data model can prove: the base codepoint occupies its cell and the combining mark does not consume a second cell (cursor advances by exactly one column for 'e' + U+0301). It does NOT assert that the accent itself survives in the snapshot -- verifying that would need a new grapheme accessor added to the JNI shim, out of scope for this task (Wave 3 files are frozen for this plan)."
